<section id="configure">
<h2>Installation is not a configured agent.</h2>
<p>The gateway needs a chat transport, model endpoint and agent catalog. The broker needs providers plus identity, policy and execution constraints. Supply credentials only to their owning process and configure telemetry collection before giving the agent useful access.</p>
<p><a class="button button-primary" href="/deploy/kubernetes/">Kubernetes installation →</a>
</p>
<p>Application <a href="{{ release.url }}">{{ release.tag }}</a> and the chart are independently versioned. Both Linux arm64 and amd64 images are published; source availability is not evidence of a healthy deployment.</p>
<p>Writing a provider rather than running an agent? Use the <a href="/guides/provider-sdk/">SDK guide</a>. The <a href="https://github.com/dekopon-agents/dekopon-console">separate console repository</a> is an optional client, not a third daemon; the chart can also run it as an idle in-pod container for <code>kubectl exec</code>, credential-free. <a href="/deploy/kubernetes/#pod">Console container</a>.</p>
</section>
